{"duration_api_ms":50245,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f0327611-e59c-4e9c-bbbd-ada9bc9354ca","total_cost_usd":1.1058384,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":113987,"cache_read_input_tokens":393032,"output_tokens":5766,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2818},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":113987,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":197278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79076},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5766,"cacheReadInputTokens":393032,"cacheCreationInputTokens":113987,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1058384,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2818,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the coder-1 labels to `labels/coder-1.json`. There is one row, `egi-draft-a1v2`, and I put Bob Heaton at **rung 4, \"Require schools to notify parents.\"**\n\n**What the chair rests on.** Heaton co-authored HB 1608 (2023). He voted Yea when the House agreed to the Senate's changes to the bill, the version that became law (Roll Call 489, 63–29). The operative section of that version says \"A school shall notify in writing at least one (1) parent of a student\" when a student asks to change their name or pronouns. That notice goes out whether or not the parents ask, so rung 3 (\"when parents ask\") doesn't fit. The final version has no requirement to get parental permission first, so rung 5 doesn't fit either. The chair rests on two sources: the enacted text and that roll call.\n\n**The other three passages, and why they don't carry the chair:**\n- **Committee version.** Heaton was still listed as a co-author after the committee amendment, and that version would have required a parent's written request before staff used a different name (rung 5). I coded it `superseded-by-later`, because the final version he voted for dropped that requirement.\n- **Third-reading vote (Roll Call 220).** I coded it `direction-only` and `superseded-by-later`. The text the House actually voted on that day isn't in the sources, so I listed it under `needs_source`.\n- **Introduced version.** It only restricted K–3 instruction and said nothing about telling parents, so I coded it `adjacent` / `off-axis`.\n\n**A call other coders might make differently.** HB 1608 has two parts: the parental-notification section and a ban on K–3 instruction about human sexuality. I treated it as a two-part bill, not an omnibus, and coded the vote `chair-shaped`. If someone reads it as `multi-subject`, the vote alone would only show a side, not a rung.\n\nNone of the sources contain Heaton's own words, so the row has no quotes.","ttft_ms":27163,"type":"result","duration_ms":51998,"uuid":"c9caa495-0cab-4f48-bf4e-1018b5f14676","ttft_stream_ms":1342,"time_to_request_ms":212,"first_content_frame_ms":1342,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
